  ('san-ignacio-belize', '10S', 'San Ignacio / Cayo, Belize', 'Belize', 'Belize''s inland adventure capital', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Belize', '{"expedition","culture","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Base for Actun Tunichil Muknal (ATM) — a guided-only Maya sacrificial cave holding the calcified ''Crystal Maiden'' skeleton near San Ignacio, Cayo District.","Xunantunich''s El Castillo (~40 m) is Belize''s 2nd-tallest structure; reached by a hand-cranked Mopan River ferry ~20 min from town.","Caracol''s Caana pyramid (141 ft / 43 m) is Belize''s tallest structure; access via military-escorted convoy from Douglas D''Silva Forest Station (~9 am) due to Guatemala-border proximity.","Blancaneaux Lodge, a ~20-room hideaway in the Mountain Pine Ridge, was bought by Francis Ford Coppola in the early 1980s and opened to guests in 1993.","BZE (Belize International) to San Ignacio is a ~2-hour drive west on the Western/George Price Highway; the Cayo caves are accessible year-round."],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (verify)","hospital":"San Ignacio Community Hospital (local); trauma to Belize City (~2 hrs) or air-medical evac to Belize City / Guatemala City (verify)","l3_disclosure":true,"stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":"BZE -> San Ignacio ~2 hr drive, Western/George Price Highway; regional airstrip Maya Flats (verify)","guatemala_border_note":"Caracol requires military-escorted convoy; Xunantunich near border — disclose, verify current","malaria":"CDC: malaria a risk in SOME parts of Belize; treat mainland jungle as potential risk, advise travel-medicine consult","dengue":"present; mosquito-bite avoidance essential","vaccines":"Hepatitis A (all 1+), typhoid (rural/smaller-city) recommended","water":"bottled/treated only; avoid swimming in fresh unchlorinated water (leptospirosis) — ATM/cave-tubing are unavoidable-immersion guided activities","founder_policy_note":"only Southside Belize City is the named dan