-salt-flats-from-san-pedro-de-atacama-2026-3-day-cross-border-tour.htm","si_tag_raw":"expedition","source_dossier":"san-pedro-de-atacama-chile","wells":["activities","move"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":15,"commission_lane":["operator","DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"}],"safety":{"status":"PENDING","reason":"the source dossier''s own safety block was written against the authority in force at the time and was dropped, not converted; awaiting the FCDO join","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/chile","read":"2026-09-01T16:18:21Z","page_updated":"2026-08-18T23:18:12+01:00","source_country":"chile","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"booking":{"advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"timing":{"peak":"year-round (driest desert; ~85-90% cloud-free)","inflection":"altiplanic winter (invierno boliviano) Jan-Feb — afternoon highland storms can close high roads; peak heat/crowds/prices; March recovers","fire_date":"booking-curve start minus 1-2 weeks (astronomy: 2-3 wks shoulder / 4-6 wks Jul-Aug)","off_season_specials":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov shoulders (milder, cheaper, thinner crowds)"},"geo":{"lat":-22.9098,"lng":-68.2001},"seo":{"meta_title":"San Pedro de Atacama & Northern Chile: Desert, Salt Flats & Stargazing Guide","search_language":"es-CL","local_keywords":["San Pedro de Atacama qué hacer","Valle de la Luna","Géiseres del Tatio","salar de Atacama","lagunas altiplánicas Miscanti Miñiques","Piedras Rojas","Laguna Cejar","tour astronómico Atacama"],"hreflang":["en","es-CL"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-20","last_verified_basis":"safety.fcdo.read","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/chile","read":"2026-08-20T14:47:39Z","source_updated":"2026-08-18T23:18:12+01:00"}]},"content_freshness":"2026-07-07","long_tail":["san pedro de atacama itinerary","el tatio geysers tour altitude","salar de atacama flamingos chaxa","altiplanic lagoons piedras rojas","atacama stargazing best time new moon","atacama luxury all inclusive lodge","calama airport to san pedro transfer"]},"source_verified":true,"ingested_from":"output/san-pedro-de-atacama-chile.md","orbit":[],"orbit_country":["chiloe-island-chile","colchagua-valley-chile","pucon-chile","santiago-chile","torres-del-paine-chile"],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to visit San Pedro De Atacama Chile?","a":"**The altiplano''s impossible colours — Miscanti, Miñiques, Piedras Rojas.** High above 4,100 m, the twin altiplanic lagoons **Miscanti and Miñiques** sit deep blue against volcanic slopes; nearby **Piedras Rojas** spills rust-red rock across white salt beside a distant peak — a full-day loop usually paired with the Salar and the village of Toconao.","source":"https://90summers.com/lagunas-miscanti-and-miniques/","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"q":"How do I get to San Pedro De Atacama Chile?","a":"**The driest desert on Earth — and its lunar valley.** Just ~15 km west of town, **Valle de la Luna** (\"Valley of the Moon\") is a protected expanse of sculpted rock, salt-crusted dunes, and formations like the Tres Marías and the Amphitheatre inside the Los Flamencos National Reserve — at its most cinematic at sunset when the Cordillera de la Sal turns pink and gold.","source":"https://chilemontana.com/blog/top-tours-and-attractions-in-san-pedro-de-atacama"