,"accessed":"2026-07-05","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":["bundle","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is climbing the pyramids hard — what''s the real risk?","a":"Altitude, sun and steps, not crime. Climbing at **~2,300 m** with steep steps and limited handrails is a cardiovascular + heat-exposure event; the site is open and shadeless. Ascend slowly with per-level rest, carry ≥1.5 L water, wear sun protection, and avoid midday climbs. If you''re already acclimatized to Mexico City you''ll feel little extra.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"safety","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"q":"Can you still climb the Pyramid of the Sun in 2026?","a":"Verify on arrival — the Sun-pyramid summit climb status is contradictory across 2026 sources. What''s confirmed: the **Pyramid of the Moon reopened for climbing on 19 May 2025**, first section only (five platforms / 47 steps), giving the best down-the-Avenue axial view.","source":"mexiconewsdaily.com, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"culture","accessed":"2026-07-05"},{"q":"Is Teotihuacán good for a couples experience?","a":"Yes — the private sunrise balloon, a champagne toast on landing, and breakfast or lunch in the **La Gruta cave restaurant ~300 m from the Pyramid of the Sun** make a natural anniversary set-piece, bookable as a full private-basket, private-guide day out of CDMX.","source":"lagruta.mx, 2026-07-05","si_tag":"romance","accessed":"2026-07-05"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Teotihuacán Sunrise Balloon & Pyramids — Day-Trip from Mexico City | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Float over the Pyramids of the Sun and Moon at sunrise, then climb the Avenue of the Dead — a UNESCO day-trip from Mexico City with certified balloon operators. Book the private experience.","search_language":"en + es-MX","hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":