":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}]},"timing":{"peak":"Year-round (event/holiday-led; inland metro)","shoulder":"Weekdays / low-event windows","green":"n/a (no coastal season; no hurricane exposure)","booking_lead":"2–6 weeks typical; 2–3 months around major GDL events","off_season_specials":"Weekday craft/culinary half-day paired with a Guadalajara city stay","event_peaks":"FIL Guadalajara book fair (late Nov/early Dec); Premio Nacional de la Cerámica (verify current-year dates)","fire_date":"6–8 weeks ahead of target GDL events; always-on evergreen for day-trip/city-break audience"},"jewels":[{"name":"Calle Independencia (Andador Independencia)","status":"future","hook":"Pedestrian gallery street — Talavera, blown glass, textiles, contemporary art","bookable_category":"tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://travelmexicosolo.com/tlaquepaque-jalisco-mexico-guide/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"culture","blurb":"Pedestrian gallery street — Talavera, blown glass, textiles, contemporary art","commission":"tour affiliate ~8–12% (guided version)","accessed":"2026-07-04","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary"},"commission_pct_low":8,"commission_pct_high":12,"commission_lane":["affiliate","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Museo Regional de la Cerámica / Premio Nacional de la Cerámica","status":"future","hook":"National ceramics-prize museum in Centro Cultural El Refugio","bookable_category":"attraction","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.afar.com/magazine/in-guadalajara-young-designers-are-putting-a-modern-spin-on-traditional-ceramics (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"culture","blurb":"National ceramics-prize museum in Centro Cultural El Refugio","commission":"via tour package only (entry non-commissionable)","accessed":"2026-07-04","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary"},"commission_lane":["package"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Tlaquepaque + Tonalá private pottery tour with clay workshop","status":"future","hook":"Hands-on half-day across both craft towns","bookable_category":"tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.pelago.com/en-US/activity/p4g83fk6p-tonala-tlaquepaque-tour-art-towns-pottery-experience-guadalajara/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"culture","blurb":"Hands-on half-day across both craft towns","commission":"tour affiliate ~8–12%","accessed":"2026-07-04","wells":["activities","shop"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary"},"commission_pct_low":8,"commission_pct_high":12,"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"El Parián","status":"future","hook":"Open-air colonial cantina — mariachi over birria and tequila, midday into night","bookable_category":"attraction","tier":"essential","source":"https://travelmexicosolo.com/tlaquepaque-jalisco-mexico-guide/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"culinary","blurb":"Open-air colonial cantina — mariachi over birria and tequila, midday into night","commission":"via food/culture tour package (walk-in dining non-commissionable)","accessed":"2026-07-04","wells":["eat","stay"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text + food SI (David 2026-10-05: every traveler has to eat)","si_all":["culinary","culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"primary","culture":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["package"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane","si_raw":"Culinary / Nightlife","si_map_basis":"normalised from free text ''Culinary / Nightlife'' by gen_normalise_jewel_si"}],"faq":[{"q":"How do I stay in the safe zone?","a":"Fly into GDL — ~11 mi / ~17 min away — and stay within the Guadalajara metro / Tlaquepaque Centro. don''t self-drive into the Jalisco interior, and keep valuables discreet in the El Parián crowds.","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Why is Tlaquepaque called Mexico''s ceramics capital?","a":"Because the craft is its living economy. With Tonalá it is one of Mexico''s two main ceramics centers, with ~2,000 artisans working clay traditions passed down since pre-Hispanic times; Calle Independencia is a pedestrian street of gallery-workshops (Talavera, blown glass, textiles), and it has been a Pueblo Mágico since October 2018.","source":"fernwayer.com / travelmexicosolo.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culture","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"q":"What should I eat and drink at El Parián?","a":"Birria, pozole, carne en su jugo and tequila. El Parián is Tlaquepaque''s iconic open-air colonial cantina — a courtyard ringed by bars with a central gazebo — where you eat Jalisco''s regional dishes over live music, ~17 minutes from the airport.","source":"travelmexicosolo.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culinary","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"q":